//! A warm checker that answers for the components a session asks about, one request at a time.
//!
//! The one-shot [`crate::resolve`] roots a single program at every component's file. A Storybook session asks about
//! one component per story, so this keeps one `tsc --api` process alive, starts it on the first request, and roots a
//! small program at just the requested files: the checker loads what those files import, not the project.
//!
//! The process runs on its own thread with its own runtime, so a caller on any thread (a NAPI worker, a rayon task)
//! never nests runtimes and can bound how long it waits. A failure to start or a crash yields an outcome with no
//! components and one diagnostic, never an error; after [`MAX_RESTARTS`] crashes the checker stays down.

use std::sync::mpsc;
use std::thread::JoinHandle;
---

**Beta re-probe (2026-10-21, `7.1.0-beta`).** `crates/tsc-client`'s smoke example spawned the beta's `bin/tsc --api`, completed the `initialize` round trip (`caseSensitivity`, `currentDirectory`) and shut down cleanly with exit status 0, so framing and shutdown behave as the fake-tsc harness assumes. `TSC_PACKAGE_DIR=<dir> cargo run -p caliper-docgen-tsc-client --example smoke_real_tsc` repeats it

**Churn.** About 20 commits touched the protocol definition (`proto.go`) between 2026-08-20 and 2026-09-18. `updateSnapshot`, project IDs and `createProgram` params were reshaped on 09-17 and 09-18. Every call the algorithm uses ran unchanged on the 09-20 and 09-26 nightlies. Re-verify on the beta.

**Freshness.** tsc sees an edit to a dependency only when told:

```js
const s1 = await s0.update({ fileNotifications: { changed: [file] }, ensurePrograms: true })
```

With the notification, the dependent component's props updated (0.5 ms update, 2.8 ms query). An unnotified disk edit stayed stale (2026-09-20). Both incremental paths must notify it once the backend is wired in: `WatchSession::update_file` and `WatchSession::ensure_fresh`, which finds changes by stat instead of being told (ADR 0007 names only the first).

